# Coach speech (Greek): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "εσύ"; the player's gender is unknown: no adjective
# or participle about the player ("έτοιμος", "σίγουρος", "κερδισμένος"); verbs instead ("Κέρδισες!",
# "κέρδιζες", "Πάμε για την επόμενη;"), or a noun ("κερδισμένη θέση" agrees with θέση).
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every line that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   neuter, with their article ("το άνοιγμα"); "{text:se}" = "στο άνοιγμα",
#                       "{text:gen}" = "του ανοίγματος" (defined in common.lang).
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement after "Ισοπαλία, {text}." ("με τριπλή επανάληψη").
#   theme.*             a "να" clause in the habitual aspect ("να κοιτάς όλη τη σκακιέρα πριν
#                       παίξεις"), said after a colon or after "προσπάθησε".
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach page's level name in « », said after "επίπεδο":
#                       "στο επίπεδο «Αρχάριος»".
# {opening} = the opening's name without article, as Greek players say it ("Παίξαμε Σικελική
# Άμυνα."); {opening:def} is not used, so the lines do not depend on the case of its article.
# Move numbers: "στην κίνηση {n}" (spoken as a neuter number). A move: "το {move}" (the commentators'
# neuter) or "την κίνηση {move}". Accuracy: "{acc:percent}" = "85%", spoken "ογδόντα πέντε τοις εκατό".
# A Greek question mark ";" does not start a sentence for the program: no piece, phase or opening
# placeholder right after one.

# ---- Names used inside the lines ------------------------------------------------------------------
appraisal.phase.opening = το άνοιγμα
appraisal.phase.middlegame = το μέσο παιχνίδι
